<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21033] lctl dk: no control on temporary raw file location</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21033</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;By default, &lt;tt&gt;lctl dk&lt;/tt&gt; uses the temporary file &lt;tt&gt;LIBCFS_DEBUG_FILE_PATH_DEFAULT&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;/tmp/lustre-log&amp;lt;EPOCH&amp;gt;.&amp;lt;pid&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;) to store raw kernel dump. This allow a distinct file for any other calls to &lt;tt&gt;lctl dk&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are some issue with this path:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;If the /tmp directory doesn't have enough space, the temporary raw file is truncated.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;If /tmp is colocated with another directory, it may fill up the filesystem with other consequences on the system.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;During the run of &lt;tt&gt;lctl dk /tmp/debugfile&lt;/tt&gt;, it takes more than the amount of disk space specified in debug_mb.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The user is not aware that it needs extra space to dump lustre kernel logs in the ASCII mode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Suggested solution:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Use &lt;tt&gt;TMPDIR&lt;/tt&gt; variable to give users the ability to choose the temporary file location&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Display the path of the temporary file&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Improve lctl man page&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

</description>
